%% Positive SRSW fixture.  glp.tex Remark "Guards and SRSW" (GLP-Spec
%% bbff21d): "if the success of a guard implies that X? is bound to a ground
%% term, then X? may occur multiple times in the clause; X occurs once, as
%% ever.  Groundness-implying guards include ground, integer, number, string,
%% constant, arithmetic comparisons (<, >, =<, >=, =:=, =\=), and ground
%% equality (=?=)."
%%
%% integer/1 is one of them, so X? twice in the body is accepted here.  Its
%% negative counterparts are srsw/known_not_ground.glp, under the
%% non-groundness-implying known/1, and srsw/ground_writer_once.glp, the
%% writer X twice under integer/1.
procedure sq(Integer?, Integer).
sq(X, Y?) :- integer(X?) | Y := X? * X?.
